.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt XFT_OS 3
.Os xft
.Sh NAME
.Nm xft_get_cpu_count
.Nd CPU count, and the private Linux system call layer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In os.h
.Ft t_result
.Fn xft_get_cpu_count "t_size *count"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn xft_get_cpu_count
stores in
.Fa *count
the number of CPUs the process may run on.
On Linux it is the population count of a 128-byte
.Xr sched_getaffinity 2
mask, so at most 1024; on Windows it is the population count of
.Ql GetProcessAffinityMask ,
so at most the 64 CPUs of the current processor group.
.Pp
.In os.h
declares only functions that have both a Linux and a Windows
implementation.
.Ss Private Linux layer
The rest of the system call wrappers are private to the library.
They are declared in
.Pa src/internal/linux/xft/xft_p_syscalls.h
and exist only on Linux; Windows code calls the win32 API directly at each
use.
This section is for working on
xft
itself.
.Pp
Each wrapper has one of three backends, chosen at build time from
.Pa src/os/linux :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa x86_64 , Pa aarch64
Freestanding.
The wrapper issues the call with inline
.Ql syscall
or
.Ql svc #0 .
Narrow enum arguments are cast to
.Vt long
at the asm operands so the whole register is loaded.
aarch64 has no legacy calls, so it uses
.Ql openat ,
.Ql mkdirat
and
.Xr clone 2
for
.Fn xft_fork ,
and passes six-argument calls through
.Fn xft_syscall6 .
.It Pa libc
.Dv XFT_REQUIRE_LIBC .
The wrapper calls
.Xr syscall 2 ;
the C library's own wrappers are not used.
64-bit arguments are cast to
.Vt long
before they reach the variadic call, so they take one slot on 32-bit
targets.
.Ql *at
variants are used where they exist, and
.Fn xft_mmap
and
.Fn xft_fmap
use
.Xr mmap2 2
when
.Dv SYS_mmap2
is defined, which is the case on 32-bit architectures.
This is the only backend for architectures other than x86_64 and aarch64.
.El
.Pp
The wrappers are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Memory
.Fn xft_mmap "size" "prot" "flags"
maps private anonymous memory,
.Fn xft_fmap "size" "prot" "flags" "fd"
maps a file at offset 0,
.Fn xft_mremap "size" "new_size" "addr" "flags_extra"
always sets
.Dv MREMAP_MAYMOVE ,
and
.Fn xft_munmap ,
.Fn xft_mprotect
and
.Fn xft_madvise "addr" "size" "advice"
pass through.
.Fn xft_mmap_commit
does nothing on Linux.
.Fn xft_map_failed
is true when a returned address lies in the last 4095 bytes of the address
space, which covers both
.Dv MAP_FAILED
and the negative error codes of the freestanding backends.
.It Files
.Fn xft_open ,
.Fn xft_close ,
.Fn xft_read ,
.Fn xft_write ,
.Fn xft_writev ,
.Fn xft_mkdir
and
.Fn xft_statx "path" "flags" "mask" "statxbuf" ,
which looks
.Fa path
up relative to the current directory with the
.Dv AT_*
lookup
.Fa flags .
.Fn xft_fcntl
takes a
.Vt t_flock ;
.Fn xft_lockf
takes a blocking shared lock over the whole file with
.Dv F_SETLKW
and
.Fn xft_unlockf
releases it.
.It Processes
.Fn xft_exit
ends the calling thread with
.Xr _exit 2
and
.Fn xft_exit_group
ends the process;
.Xr xft_exit_process 3
is the public, portable form of the latter.
.Fn xft_getpid ,
.Fn xft_wait4 ,
.Fn xft_prlimit64 ,
which reads or sets a resource limit through a
.Vt t_rlimit
of two 64-bit words on every architecture,
.Fn xft_set_tid_address
and
.Fn xft_clone ,
which takes a
.Vt t_clone_arg
and resumes the child on its stack without calling an entry function.
.Fn xft_fork
issues
.Xr fork 2
on freestanding x86_64 and
.Xr clone 2
with only
.Dv XFT_SIGCHLD
elsewhere.
.It Threads and time
.Fn xft_futex_wait
and
.Fn xft_futex_wake
issue
.Dv FUTEX_WAIT
and
.Dv FUTEX_WAKE
without
.Dv FUTEX_PRIVATE_FLAG
or a timeout.
.Fn xft_clock_gettime
reads
.Dv CLOCK_MONOTONIC .
.Fn xft_sched_getaffinity
and
.Fn xft_sched_setaffinity
take a mask of
.Vt t_u64a
words.
.It Performance counters
.Fn xft_perf_event_open
and
.Fn xft_ioctl
back the
.Pa perf
subproject.
.El
.Pp
The constants are typed enums with an
.Ql xft_
prefix, such as
.Dv xft_prot_read ,
.Dv xft_map_private ,
.Dv xft_o_creat ,
.Dv xft_at_symlink_nofollow
and
.Dv xft_statx_btime ,
declared in
.Pa src/internal/linux/xft/types/xft_p_syscalls_types.h
together with the system call numbers for x86_64 and aarch64 and the
.Vt t_clone_arg ,
.Vt t_flock
and
.Vt t_statx
structures.
The prefix keeps them from colliding with the C library's macros of the
same names.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xft_get_cpu_count
returns
.Dv OK ,
or
.Dv KO
if the affinity mask cannot be read.
.Pp
The private wrappers that return an integer give the non-negative result of
the call on success and \-1 on failure.
The error code is dropped by the freestanding backends and left in
.Va errno
by the libc backend.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xft_files 3 ,
.Xr xft_io 3 ,
.Xr xft_rt 3 ,
.Xr xft_signals 3 ,
.Xr xft_timing 3 ,
.Xr xft 7
.Sh CAVEATS
32-bit Linux is supported through the libc backend only.
.Xr clock_gettime 2
uses
.Dv SYS_clock_gettime ,
which 32-bit musl does not provide.
